  "security_implications": "ctrl_err_storage_q acts as a sticky error flag likely used to gate AES operations or escalate faults. Once set, it stays high until reset, preventing normal operation and possibly blocking access to sensitive data paths. The lack of a non-reset clear path means a transient fault could permanently lock the AES core, requiring a system reset. This is security-relevant because it controls error containment and may influence alert escalation or key-flow gating.",
